          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %strong Hypothesis H
            is a hypothesis about the mathematical formulation of the theory of fundamental physics known as
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge+quantization"} charge quantization
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            happens in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+cohomology"} non-abelian cohomology
            theory called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomotopy"} cohomotopy
            (in more detail:
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomotopy"} twisted cohomotopy
            %a{:href => "#Sati13"} Sati 2013
            (
            %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1310.1060.pdf#page=17"}> Sec. 2.5
            ) and has become the theme of a research program developed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#References"} below
          %p
            (In a play on how the “M” in “M-theory” has been
            %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/M-theory#MagicMysteryQuote"} said
            to be either for “Membrane” or for “Mystery”, so the “H” in “Hypothesis H” may be read as being either for “Homotopy” or for “Hisham”.)
          %h2#TheOpenProblemOfFormulatingMTheory The open problem of formulating M-Theory
          %p
            It is an open problem to mathematically formulate
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theory of physics
            whose various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+of+a+sequence"} limiting
            cases reproduce the zoo of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"} perturbative string theories
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"}> HET
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+I+string+theory"}> I
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"}> IIA
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+string+theory"}> IIB
            \&amp;
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"}> F
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D11+supergravity"}> 11d SuGra
            ) and the expected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} dualities
            relating them; but which also makes mathematical sense of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} non-perturbative
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-brane"} M-brane
            physics, and hence solves, via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+Yang-Mills+theory"} quantum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"}> holographic QCD
            ), the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+gap+problem"} last of the Millennium Problems
          %center
            %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/Schreiber-MTheoryMathematics2020-v200126.pdf#page=8"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/ProblemQCDToProblemM230120.jpg", :width => "670"}/
          %p
            In the
            = succeed "-minded" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            community, parts of the literature tends to forget or downplay the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjecture"} conjectural
            nature of many assumptions and leaps of faiths that are being made when it comes to discussion of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-brane"} M-brane
            dynamics and generally of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effects"} non-perturbative effects
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+branes"} coincident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            is missing, together with the formulation of its expected decoupling limit to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D6+N%3D%282%2C0%29+SCFT"} D=6 N=(2,0) SCFT
            – but of course these major open problems are but one aspect of full
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/M-theory#TheOpenProblem"} M-theory – The open problem
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+with+one+element"} field with one element
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analogy"} analogy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theories"} perturbative string theories
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"}> HET
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+I+string+theory"} I
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} IIA
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+string+theory"} IIB
            and their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactified
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory+vacua"} perturbative string theory vacua
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometries
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} base
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+fields"} prime fields
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_p
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \geq 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            corresponds to a theory of a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+with+one+element"}> field with one element
            ” that unifies and completes all this, by describing it at a deeper level (literally: a deeper base).
          %p
            Hence the task here is to conjure a mathematical theory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            %em is
            the putative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            in order to check to which extent they include the required design criterion “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi ST
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X} \Rightarrow ST
            ”. To the extent that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            implies known or expected phenomena in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"} perturbative string theory
            the hypothesis that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            %em is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            finds support, to the extent that it doesn’t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            needs to be modified to or be replaced by some
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}'
          %h2#hypothesis_h Hypothesis H
          %h3#StatementOfHypothesisH Statement
          %p
            In the large-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scale"}> scale
            \/low-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy"} energy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+of+a+sequence"} limit
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            given by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D11+supergravity"} D=11 supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            must consist of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+constraints+in+supergravity"} super-torsion free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartan+geometry"} super orbi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{10,1\vert \mathbf{32}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V-manifold"} -folds
            equipped with a suitable
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+field"} higher gauge field
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
          %center
            %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/Schreiber-MTheoryMathematics2020-v200126.pdf#page=12"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/MTheoryInSupergravityLimit200123.jpg", :width => "670"}/
          %p
            The first ingredient of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} non-perturbative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantization
            of this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            must be a choice of
            = succeed "-condition" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac charge quantization
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
          %center
            %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/Schreiber-MTheoryMathematics2020-v200126.pdf#page=14"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/HypothesisH200123.jpg", :width => "670"}/
          %p#HypothesisH
            %strong Hypothesis H:
            (
            %a{:href => "#FSS19b"}> FSS 19b
            ,
            %a{:href => "#FSS19c"}> FSS 19c
            )
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} charge quantized
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-homomorphism"} J-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomotopy"} twisted
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomotopy+cohomology+theory"} cohomotopy cohomology theory
          %center
            %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/Schreiber-MTheoryMathematics2020-v200126.pdf#page=21"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/HypothesisH.jpg", :width => "640"}/
          %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
            %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1903.02834.pdf#page=14"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/TheRational4SphereAppears.jpg", :width => "380"}/
          %h3#MotivationFromHomotopyTheoreticReanalysisOfBraneScan Motivation from homotopy theoretic re-analysis of the brane-scan
          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "#HypothesisH"} Hypothesis H
            (
            %a{:href => "#StatementOfHypothesisH"}> above
            ) is motivated from re-analysis (based on
            %a{:href => "#Sati13"} Sati 13, Sec. 2.5
            see
            %a{:href => "#FSS19a"} FSS 19a
            for comprehensive review) of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes"} super p-brane WZ terms
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+homotopy+theory"} super homotopy theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/brane+bouquet"} brane bouquet
            %em proves
            that – in the approximation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            –
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-brane"} M-brane
            charge is in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+cohomotopy"} rational cohomotopy
            in exactly the same way that
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge+quantization+in+K-theory"} D-brane charge is in twisted K-theory
          %p
            %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1606.03206.pdf#page=20"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/SupercocyclesRationalTwistedKTheory.jpg", :width => "440"}/
          %p
            Detailed lecture note on this point are at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes"} geometry of physics – fundamental super p-branes
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes#MFluxFields"} M-Flux fields
          %hr/
          %center
            %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/EquivariantSuperHomotopyTheory120314a.pdf#page=74"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/BraneBouquetAnimated.gif", :width => "450 />"}/
          %h2#Implications Implications
          %p
            Assuming
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HypothesisH"} Hypothesis H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            and may rigorously derive properties of the resulting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/states"} states
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#HypothesisH"} Hypothesis H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"} perturbative string theory
            and to the extent that they match
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folklore"} folklore
            about
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a{:href => "#HypothesisH"} Hypothesis H
            finds support, to the extend that they do not
            %a{:href => "#HypothesisH"} Hypothesis H
            may need to be adjusted or abandoned.
          %h3#anomaly_cancellation Anomaly cancellation
          %p
            What physicists call
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomalies"} anomalies
            are what mathematician call
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstructions"} obstructions
            to the construction of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} physical theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomaly+cancellation"} cancellation
            of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomalies"} anomalies
            in every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folklore"} folklore
            expects to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+of+a+sequence"} limiting case
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            is strictly necessary for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            to exist: Any remaining anomaly is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
            against the existence of the theory that it is an anomaly of.
          %p A long list of anomaly cancellation conditions in M-theory has been argued for in the literature, obtained from a variety of different arguments and under various assumptions, but supported by a web of consistency checks.
          %p
            %strong Theorem
            (
            %a{:href => "#FSS19b"}> FSS 19b
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FSS19c"} FSS 19c
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#SS19a"} SS 19a
          %p
            %em>
              %a{:href => "##HypothesisH"} Hypothesis H
              implies the following list of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomaly+cancellation"} anomaly cancellation
              consistency conditions expected in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folklore"} folklore
            \:
          %center
            %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1904.10207.pdf#page=2"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/HypothesisHImplications.jpg", :width => "740"}/
          %h4#OnCurvedButNonSingularManifolds On curved but non-singular 8-manifolds
          %p
            Here is a quick survey of the implications of
            %em
              %a{:href => "#HypothesisH"} Hypothesis H
            on expected M-theory anomaly cancellation conditions for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+8-manifolds"} M-theory on 8-manifolds
          %p
            %strong download:
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/files/HypothesisHIntroductionAndSurvey191125.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %center
            %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1904.10207.pdf#page=2"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/AnmlCnclltnInMThryOn8MfdsViaHypothesisH.jpg", :width => "740"}/
          %h4#on_flat_but_singular_orbifolds On flat but singular orbifolds:
          %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
            %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1909.12277.pdf#page=5"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/AbsoluteDBraneOPlaneCharge.jpg", :width => "500"}/
          %p
            %a{:href => "#HypothesisH"} Hypothesis H
            implies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field+tadpole+cancellation"} RR-field tadpole cancellation
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+orbifolds"} flat orbifolds
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularities"} ADE-singularities
            %em absolute
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O-plane+charge"} O-plane charge
            and hence the
            = succeed "-" do
